{"@context":["https://litlfred.github.io/folio-assistant/ns/content/v1.jsonld",{"@base":"https://litlfred.github.io/folio/","folio-assistant-sci":"https://litlfred.github.io/folio-assistant-sci/v0/ns/"}],"@id":"papers/quantum-observable-universe/blocks/def-demand-profile","@type":["folio-assistant-sci:Definition","doco:Section"],"label":"def:demand-profile","kind":"definition","title":"Demand profile of a derived atom","uses":["papers/quantum-observable-universe/blocks/def-derived-atom"],"tags":["demand","normal-form","stability","derived-atom"],"leanRef":"qou:QOU.ParticleInteractions.demandProfile","text":"demand-profile.md","leanSource":"demand-profile.lean","provenance":"authored","html":"<a id=\"def:demand-profile\"></a><p><em>Let <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">\\mathcal{A}(Z, N) = \\sum_w c_w \\cdot w</code> be a derived atom in normal form. Its <strong>demand profile</strong> is</em></p>\n<pre><code class=\"language-math math-display\">  \\mathrm{dem}(\\mathcal{A})\n  \\;=\\;\n  \\{(w, c_w) : c_w &#x3C; 0\\}\n  \\;\\subset\\;\n  \\mathrm{NF}(B_A) \\times \\mathbb{R}_{&#x3C;0}.</code></pre>\n<p><em>The <strong>demand magnitude</strong> is <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">|\\mathrm{dem}| = \\sum_{c_w &#x3C; 0} |c_w|</code>.</em></p>\n","source":"folio/quantum-observable-universe/nuclear-interactions/demand-profile.md","heading":"Definition","number":"14.4.1","page":"b/def-demand-profile","qa":{"counts":{"pass":81,"fail":0,"warn":0,"na":10,"unknown":0,"stale":63},"milnor":{"total":3,"notPassing":0}},"lean":{"expected":true,"ref":"qou:QOU.ParticleInteractions.demandProfile","via":"sibling","path":"folio/quantum-observable-universe/nuclear-interactions/demand-profile.lean","compiles":"unchecked","sorry":false,"sorryBasis":"text"}}
